zation only (0.173834ms)\n✔ failed update leaves cached lists in place (0.159042ms)\n✔ organization IDs sharing prefixes or containing punctuation stay separate (0.329083ms)\n✔ authenticated detail (0.57675ms)\n✔ authenticated list (5.164709ms)\n✔ update then read (0.127708ms)\n✔ anonymous request rejected (0.322375ms)\n✔ invalid update rejected (0.070708ms)\nℹ tests 18\nℹ pass 18\nℹ fail 0\n M src/cache/keys.ts\n M src/services/project-service.ts\n?? tests/isolation.test.ts","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfhNqbgdDvbS5Dz51gN52","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All three reported bugs are fixed, and the full suite passes (18 tests: the 8 existing ones, unmodified, plus 10 new ones). Nothing is committed.\n\n## Root causes and fixes\n\n- **Cross-organization read/update** (`src/services/project-service.ts`): project reads and updates never checked membership. They now require membership in the project's actual owning organization, so nonmembers get 403 `{error:\"forbidden\"}`. The check runs before body validation and before any write, and organization IDs supplied in the body are ignored.\n- **Wrong organization's list after switching** (`src/cache/keys.ts`): the list cache key left out the organization ID, so every organization shared the same entries. The key now includes the organization ID along with page, page size, sort and direction.\n- **Stale list after update** (`src/services/project-service.ts`): an update only cleared an unused detail key. A successful update now deletes every cached list for the owning organization and leaves other organizations' entries alone.\n\nThe organization ID is JSON-quoted inside the key, so IDs that share prefixes or contain punctuation (`org`, `org:1`, `org:1:10`) cannot collide or be invalidated together.\n\nThe list route already checked membership before consulting the cache; I left that in place, so cache hits remain authorized and a revoked membership takes effect immediately. Caching stays enabled, and API signatures, response shapes and status codes are unchanged.\n\n## Verification\n\n`npm test` runs the new `tests/isolation.test.ts` alongside the existing files. The new tests cover:\n\n- A nonmember reading or updating a project gets 403, with storage, the update counter and cache keys unchanged.\n- 404 for a missing project and 401 for an anonymous request still apply.\n- A nonmember listing gets 403, including when the list is already cached, and after membership is revoked.\n- Switching organizations returns the right projects, and a repeated list is served from cache.\n- Page, page size, sort and direction variants are cached separately; a repeated request makes no new repository query and returns the same response shape.\n- An update invalidates all four cached variants of the owning organization, while the other organization's four variants are still served from cache.\n- A rejected (400) update leaves cached lists in place.\n- Organization IDs with shared prefixes and punctuation stay isolated in both caching and invalidation."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4770,"cache_read_input_tokens":16554,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4770},"output_tokens":639,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a7c4d0e5-6921-4413-bd4d-8b16555cdff9","uuid":"794c2455-7a84-4d45-ba26-20f8558d4e25","timestamp":"2026-10-04T14:45:41.692Z","request_id":"req_011CfhNqaxEMRidsdN9EPyto"}
